{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Both straw and fodder</b> — which you did not ask for; <b>also a place</b> — which you did ask for. Also, to include his own needs and the needs of the men who are with him." "<b>To lodge.</b> עצמכם, like לדון, לשוב, לקום — to say that there is no special inn for a person to be hosted in, in the usual manner, but there is a place for him to lodge with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:35.806498360Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}